    "updated_at": "2023-06-29T07:32:14Z",
    "body": "I'd say `fmap.draw()` producing the text output is fine because it allows for use without installing matplotlib and pylatexenc.\r\n\r\nRegarding producing a matplotlib plot, `fmap.draw(output=\"mpl\")` already works. If we want to make `fmap.draw(\"mpl\")` work, we need to pass `*args` to the qiskit routine (which then requires `feature_label`, `parameter_label` and `decompose` to be set), or do some other fancy argument handling.\r\n\r\nThoughts @David-Kreplin ?",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
    "pin": null,
